.TH NAMTOR-CLI 1 "2026-09-16" "namtor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
namtor\-cli \- enrol and manage Nam-tor face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B namtor\-cli
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B namtor\-cli
is the terminal front-end to
.BR namtor\-daemon (8).
It enrols face templates, lists and removes enrolments, runs a one-shot
verification and collects a privacy-safe support bundle.
.PP
Commands talk to the daemon over the system bus by default. The
.B \-\-local
flag on
.B list
and
.B remove
selects a direct-store recovery path that does not need a running daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report the selected device, stream state and protection level.
.TP
.B enroll
Enrol a face template using the daemon-driven continuous enrollment
lifecycle: start, watch live progress, press Enter to stop, then Save,
Resume or Discard at the review step.
.B SIGINT
discards cleanly.
.TP
.B verify
Verify a face against the enrolled templates via the daemon socket.
.TP
.B list
List enrolled profiles.
.TP
.B remove \fIUID\fP [\fIPROFILE_ID\fP]
Remove an enrolment.
.I PROFILE_ID
defaults to
.IR default .
.TP
.B diagnostics
Write a privacy-safe diagnostics support bundle.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
Act on another user's enrolment
.RB ( enroll ", " verify ).
Requires root.
.TP
.B \-\-old
Use the local capture-and-store enrollment flow instead of the daemon
lifecycle. Kept for daemon-less environments.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Use the direct-store recovery path instead of the daemon
.RB ( list ", " remove ).
.TP
.BI \-\-out\-dir " DIR"
Destination directory for
.BR diagnostics .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/namtor/templates
Encrypted enrolled face templates.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed; a diagnostic is printed on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR namtor\-daemon (8)
